<title>USA: No cold weather seen for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>No cold weather seen for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A low pressure system off the coast of Uruguay is expected to move out to sea during the next 48-72 hours, taking with it any cold weather that could have hit Brazil's coffee belt, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Monday.</p>
<p>According to WSC, a weak surface high behind the low pressure system is expected to linger over the region.</p>
<p>Rain and thunderstorms were seen across the coffee belt over the weekend. Temperatures averaged near to above normal with lows ranging from 48-58 F (9-15 C).</p>
<p>Lingering showers are expected throughout the region today. Mostly fair skies are in the forecast for tomorrow and Wednesday. Temperatures should range from the upper 40's to the upper 50's F (9-15 C).</p>
<p>The extended outlook calls for mostly fair weather and above normal temperatures through Sunday.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
